    backlog:gapsObjective pcl:Obj3_A10,
        pcl:Obj3_A4a,
        pcl:Obj3_A5,
        pcl:Obj3_A6a,
        pcl:Obj3_A6b,
        pcl:Obj3_A8a,
        pcl:Obj3_A8b,
        pcl:Obj3_A9 ;
    backlog:hasFitGapStatement "As-is on 2026-11-08. Done (7 stories): the stand-alone ontology (S1), its tree of kinds (S2), the qualities and their standards (S3), the 28 rules (S4), the default page format (S9), the move to IPage (S14) and the one browser measurement (S15); their deliverables hold as measured. Cancelled (8 stories, 4 epics, 1 task; 1 iteration dissolved): rules as shapes (S5: built, but the three reviews of 2026-11-08 found the shapes never refuse a page in the project's own checks and do not name the rule), rules as Stage 4 gates (S6), the check of the shipped pages (S7), a page for every profile (S8), the course page as one profile's page (S10, S11), the measured release path (S12) and the hand-over (S13). Every objective is read again at closure (the closing observations); those short of target are recorded Missed: rules as gates, shipped pages failing, profiles without a page statement, profile shapes, the two course-page checks, the hand-over, and the release-path figure."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasImpactStatement "Closing now loses nothing recorded: the delivered stories stay Done and measured; the cancelled work and the defects found in S5 pass as scope to narrow Delivery lineages, the repair of the rule shapes first; the two pending hand-overs (how an epic closes; whether a profile may name its own page format) pass to IPage's Governance lineage. Keeping Lineage 3 open would hold a package-wide mission open while its slices are built one at a time, which the Owner's rule on narrow lineages refuses, and a mission can only be widened, never narrowed."^^xsd:string .

