pcl:Finding3_BuildBeforeStart_S1_S2 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The first build of S1, S2 was made before its start was recorded"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-04T10:03:56+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Disclosed here and not backfilled. Nothing was released before this record; the build is released together with it, and Done is recorded only after the acceptance criteria hold."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The two stories are tied (a new ontology file must have every class linked), so the file was built in one piece in the working tree, and the step script that records a start did not yet exist for this lineage."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem pcl:Story3_S1,
        pcl:Story3_S2 .

pcl:Finding3_Close_1 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The 28 rule shapes never refused a page in the project's own checks"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Carried forward, first in order, to the Delivery lineage on rules as checks: core targets (or the advanced mode in every call), and a test in which a page that breaks a rule is refused through the exact command the gate runs."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Each shape selects its targets with a SPARQL target, a SHACL advanced feature the validator applies only in its advanced mode; the release check, the measurement's self-test and the criterion's own command run it without that mode, and the self-test tried only a page built to pass. Found by the approving and verifying agents on 2026-11-08 on a fresh clone at commit e3be984: in advanced mode a breaking page is refused (36 violations for 18 failing rules); without it the same page conforms."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_2 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "A refused page's report does not name the rule"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Carried forward with the first finding: each rule's message and name on the check that fails, tested with results whose identifiers carry no rule number."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Each rule's message sits on the outer node shape while the failing check is an unnamed inner property shape, so the report shows the validator's generic text; the rule shows only through the result's identifier, which the measurement happens to build from the rule number. Found by the overseeing agent on 2026-11-08."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_3 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The rule shapes need the rule records loaded with them"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Carried forward: the gate's command loads the vocabulary and the records together, and the Delivery lineage's test proves it."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "A result names its rule by a link to a rule record in the A-Box; validating with the T-Box alone refuses every result (56 'not a page rule' violations), so every check must load both. Found by the verifying agent on 2026-11-08."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_4 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "A figure that counted the link, not the effect"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The Delivery lineage measures rules whose shape refuses a planted breaking page through the gate's own command."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Objective A3c counts shapes that carry a link to a rule. It read 28 of 28 while no shape had ever refused a page in the project's own checks, so it could not fall when the shapes did not work: completion is not accomplishment."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_5 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Guard figures were recorded from missing inputs"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Corrected here, not rewritten there: read again at closure with the register and the full history; measure_page_ontology 2.2.0 finds the register by default, bounds X1 at the move and refuses a shallow clone."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The readings of Conf, Contained and X1 recorded at the finish of S9 and S15 were -1 because the measurement ran without the register (Conf, Contained) or without the monorepo's history (X1); the note of the S9 measurement called -1 the metrics' documented meaning, which was wrong: it was a missing input. X1 also counted the rdodi-ecosystem session's own releases after the move (6 files of oe-pack), and X4 read 4 from a shallow clone and 0 from the full history."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_6 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Forty-six objective queries name a path that no longer exists"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Not rewritten in a concluded lineage; the new lineages state their own commands."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "The stored measurement command of 46 objectives still names the monorepo path and measure_page_ontology_v1_0_0.py, from before the move to IPage. Found by the overseeing agent on 2026-11-08."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_7 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "An obstacle that stopped work was never raised"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Resolved by cancelling the epic (option 3 of the hand-over) on the Owner's ruling IP-R1; the hand-over's remaining question, how an epic closes as Done, passes to IPage's Governance lineage."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Closing S5 was blocked from 2026-11-05 by the rule that an epic resolves when its last child does (G148); the block lived only in a hand-over, not as an impediment with its kind and owner (G191)."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_Close_8 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "The release-path figure counts every commit that is not a release"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-08T09:05:49+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "The Delivery lineages measure changes that reached a release without the gate, not commits between releases."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Objective A9 counts commits that are neither a release nor a hand-over deposit (17 at closure); the lineage discipline's own practice commits each stage and step before its release, so the figure counts that practice as well as any real bypass."^^xsd:string .

pcl:Finding3_IneffectiveMaintenanceMetrics_S3_S4_S14_S15 a backlog:RetrospectiveFinding ;
    rdfs:label "Taking the first bracketing reading for the lineage's broad maintenance metrics (Conf, Contained, X1-X6, A9) exposes drift against stories closed before any such reading existed"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage pcl:Lineage03 ;
    backlog:detectedAt "2026-11-05T12:05:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    backlog:detectedBy backlog:Builder ;
    backlog:hasFindingScope backlog:Scope_LineageLocal ;
    backlog:hasRemedy "Disclosed here, not interpreted or fixed. Recording that the pattern was seen and considered is what this shape requires; deciding whether to narrow metricMovableBy to the objectives each story actually pursues, or to leave the broad linkage and expect this kind of drift on every future first-reading, is the Owner's or the framework's call, not this session's to make unasked."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasRootCause "Obj3_Conf, Obj3_Contained, Obj3_X1 through Obj3_X6 and Obj3_A9 all hold backlog:metricMovableBy links to every story of this lineage, S3, S4 and S14 included, as a blanket default recorded when the register was built -- not because each of those stories specifically targeted these broad maintenance/exclusion-tracking metrics. No observation of any of these objectives existed at or after any of those stories' own finishedAt until Story S15's finish recorded one (needed to satisfy CorrectiveActionMeasuredOnCloseShape for Story S15 itself, which shares the same metricMovableBy links). That one new reading is now the nearest 'after' observation for S3, S4 and S14 too, and for at least one of these Hold-direction objectives it differs from the reading that was nearest their own start -- which is what IneffectiveCorrectiveAttemptAdvisoryShape/CorrectiveActionMeasuredOnCloseShape detect. This is a structural consequence of the blanket metricMovableBy linkage finally being checked for the first time, not a defect introduced by Story S15's own work, and not a claim that any of these four stories failed at something they were trying to do. Story S9's own finish records a second such reading, sharing the same blanket metricMovableBy links, and the same drift against the same pre-existing baseline recurs for the same structural reason; it is added to this finding rather than opened as a new one, since the root cause and remedy are identical."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:relatesToWorkItem pcl:Story3_S14,
        pcl:Story3_S15,
        pcl:Story3_S3,
        pcl:Story3_S4,
        pcl:Story3_S9 .

