    backlog:hasRationale "Baseline read by the measurement script on 2026-11-04; the target follows from the scope deliverable it serves, not from a wish. The counting rules are checked by the script's self-test. The 28 rules counted: 1. Menu clicks change the main area first; 2. The right-hand detail card appears only when a detail is explicitly requested; 3. Tab menus are always sub-menus of the selected top-level item, never mixed with it; 4. Code on the page really runs: edited code changes the result; 5. Subject agents answer from their own slice of the ontology and corpus, not with generic identical answers; 6. Every diagram has zoom in and out, a full-screen view and a resizable panel; 7. The top-level menu stays uncrowded; 8. No list is shown twice on one screen; 9. Static explanations live in their own sub-tabs or in the detail card; 10. A taxonomy is drawn as one connected tree with labels that fit their boxes; 11. The page adapts to any device and screen, from a phone to a large screen, and scales as the window is resized; 12. Default text is not small; 13. The reader can adjust the text size; 14. Zoom controls never cover the diagram; 15. Touching a content element shows its options first, preferably in the right-hand card; 16. There is no third level of sub-tabs (a breadcrumb is used instead); 17. Choosing a low-level item in the left explorer opens that single item, not its siblings; 18. The tabs and the left hierarchical explorer always stay synchronized; 19. Every term and tool used on the page is explained; 20. Explanations are comprehensive, cohesive paragraphs of full sentences; 21. Learn sections carry visualizations and interactions, not rich text alone; 22. Long explanations are divided into sub-pages with direct access to each; 23. The concept map is readable and offers filtering; 24. The ontology graph shows its syntactic, semantic and behavioural categorizations; 25. Content and visualizations fit the display without scrolling; 26. Meta information about the work itself is guidance only and is never shown as content; 27. The top of the screen is never spent cheaply: tooltips replace messages and accordions, with details in the right-hand card; 28. Visualizations and interactions are merged with the content, and nothing sits behind a click a reader would only find by chance. The Owner's instructions on slides and course content are not page rules and are not counted. A different count found when the rules are collected is a gap and enters through change management."^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasSuccessMetric "Count of the Owner's page rules recorded as rules in the stand-alone ontology (28 counted by the session on 2026-11-04)"^^xsd:string ;
    backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasTargetValue 28.0 ;
    backlog:metricMovableBy pcl:Story3_S4 .

